cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BooFun in your research, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "BooFun: Boolean Function Analysis in Python"
authors:
  - family-names: Taboada
    given-names: Gabriel
    affiliation: "University of California, Berkeley"
    # TODO: register an ORCID iD and add it here before JOSS submission:
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX"
version: 1.3.0
date-released: 2026-07-25
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/GabbyTab/boofun"
url: "https://gabbytab.github.io/boofun/"
keywords:
  - boolean functions
  - fourier analysis
  - property testing
  - query complexity
  - theoretical computer science
  - python
abstract: >-
  BooFun is an open-source Python library for creating, transforming, and
  analyzing Boolean functions. It provides a notebook-oriented interface for
  Fourier analysis, influence and sensitivity measures, query complexity,
  property testing, hypercontractivity, learning-theoretic algorithms, and
  cryptographic metrics. Multiple representations share a common API, and
  numerical implementations are validated against closed-form results,
  redundant computation paths, and independent software.
